{#
/**
 * @file
 * Template for the Form embed component.
 *
 * Renders an empty div for the vendor's script to write the form into, and
 * beside it an alert naming the form, saying why it isn't there, and linking
 * to it. form-embed.js loads the script, using the handler the vendor's
 * submodule adds to this component's library.
 *
 * This template only displays what it's given, and calls nothing from a
 * module. The addresses arrive already checked: from the media item's
 * az_form_embed_form field when Canvas renders it, or from az_form_embed's
 * formatter in the page builder. Both get them from the vendor that accepted
 * the link.
 *
 * Keep the alert outside the div. Rationale: a vendor's script replaces
 * everything inside it. For example, if Slate can't fetch the form, it
 * overwrites the div with its own "To complete this form, click here."
 * message, so a link inside would vanish right when someone needs it. The
 * loading spinner goes inside the div for the same reason: the form replaces
 * it.
 *
 * The link goes to the form's plain address, not the embed address. A vendor
 * answers the embed address with JavaScript, so a link to it would show a
 * script instead of the form.
 *
 * The alert is visible here in the markup. The loader hides it once it takes
 * over, and shows it again if the form fails, so a browser with no JavaScript
 * still gets the link. That browser is also the only one that reads the
 * reason written below, because the loader replaces it in every other case.
 *
 * The retry button ends the sentence and looks like the link below it. It's
 * a button, not a link, because it loads the form again in place instead of
 * going anywhere. The loader shows it only when the form took too long to
 * arrive. The cause is usually a slow server, such as Slate's test server
 * waking up, and a second try often works.
 *
 * Two openings are written and the stylesheet shows one. The plain one is for
 * a visitor, and doesn't name the form, because its name means nothing to
 * them. The loader asks for the named one, by adding --names-form, when the
 * reason is something a person can act on.
 *
 * In Canvas's editor and its Preview page, the live form loads too, so
 * editors see the real form. Only CKEditor and the Media Library show the
 * Form embed placeholder instead, and az_form_embed's formatter decides that.
 *
 * Props:
 * - form.vendor: The vendor's machine name, such as slate. The loader runs
 *   that vendor's handler.
 * - form.embed_url: The address the vendor's embed script loads from.
 * - form.canonical_url: The form's plain address, safe to link to.
 * - form.label: The media item's name. The placeholder filter puts it in as
 *   Drupal's own em.placeholder, so the sentence stays one translatable
 *   string, and the loader can read the name back out of that element.
 * - utility_classes: Additional Bootstrap utility classes for the outer
 *   wrapper, such as mb-5.
 *
 * Renders nothing without an embed address, except in Canvas's editor. There
 * the placeholder's icon shows until a form is picked, so the editor can see
 * and select the component. Canvas passes canvas_is_preview to every
 * component it renders. Reading it needs nothing from Canvas, and elsewhere
 * it's simply undefined.
 */
#}
{% set attributes = attributes|default(create_attribute()) %}
{% set vendor = form.vendor|default('') %}
{% set embed_url = form.embed_url|default('') %}
{% set canonical_url = form.canonical_url|default('') %}
{% set label = form.label|default('') %}
{% set utility_classes = utility_classes|default([]) %}
{# If a caller passes one class as a string, wrap it in a list. The schema asks
   for a list, but Drupal only checks that while PHP assertions are on, which
   they aren't in production. #}
{% if utility_classes is not iterable %}
  {% set utility_classes = [utility_classes] %}
{% endif %}

{% if embed_url and vendor %}
  <div{{ attributes.addClass('az-form-embed', ('az-form-embed--' ~ vendor)|clean_class, utility_classes) }}>
    <div class="az-form-embed__form" data-az-form-embed-vendor="{{ vendor }}" data-az-form-embed-src="{{ embed_url }}"></div>
    <div class="az-form-embed__fallback alert alert-warning" role="alert">
      <p class="az-form-embed__message">
        <span class="az-form-embed__icon" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span>
        <span class="az-form-embed__opening az-form-embed__opening--plain">{{ 'A form couldn\'t load'|t }}</span>
        <span class="az-form-embed__opening az-form-embed__opening--named">{% trans %}The form {{ label|placeholder }} was not embedded{% endtrans %}</span>
        <span class="az-form-embed__reason">{{ 'because this browser has JavaScript turned off.'|t }}</span>
        <button type="button" class="az-form-embed__retry alert-link" hidden>
          {{- 'Try again'|t }}
          <svg class="az-form-embed__link-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
               viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
               stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
               aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <polyline points="23 4 23 10 17 10"/>
            <path d="M20.49 15a9 9 0 1 1-2.12-9.36L23 10"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </p>
      <a href="{{ canonical_url }}" class="az-form-embed__link alert-link" rel="noopener">
        {{ 'Open the form'|t }}
        <svg class="az-form-embed__link-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
             viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
             aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/>
          <polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/>
          <line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
{% elseif canvas_is_preview|default(false) %}
  {{ include('az_quickstart:form-embed-placeholder', {}, with_context = false) }}
{% endif %}
